External textures on the Metal backend (ADR-0058, decision 2 and step b); ADR-0029, decision 8).

Why: SurfaceTexture, video players, camera previews and Flutter's textures sample their frames through
samplerExternalOES on GL_TEXTURE_EXTERNAL_OES, whose EGL image Minato makes of an AHardwareBuffer's IOSurface.
The Metal backend kept GL_OES_EGL_image_external and its ESSL 3 variant off, its MSL translator left
samplerExternalOES unimplemented, and TextureMtl::setEGLImageTarget refused an External texture for a 2D image.
Now both extensions are on, samplerExternalOES is a texture2d in MSL with the 2D sampler's prelude functions,
and an External texture adopts a 2D image (EGL_METAL_TEXTURE_ANGLE), as a 2D texture on Metal.
Upstream: could go upstream; the Vulkan backend has both extensions (vk_caps_utils.cpp).
Remove: when upstream's Metal backend supports external images.

